{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september","id":1514142,"title":"Paradox will make a Bloodlines 2 announcement in September","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-07T16:01:05-07:00","id":1514142,"title":"Paradox will make a Bloodlines 2 announcement in September","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/VtM_Bloodlines/status/1666403803090886658?t=KmKnUC_-Oe68zOfVnbnk2w&amp;s=19\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/FyA44U8XwAEUDwv?format=webp&amp;name=large\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/VtM_Bloodlines/status/1666403803090886658?t=KmKnUC_-Oe68zOfVnbnk2w&amp;s=19\" target=\"_blank\"> Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2 (@VtM_Bloodlines) on X </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/VtM_Bloodlines/status/1666403803090886658?t=KmKnUC_-Oe68zOfVnbnk2w&amp;s=19\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/VtM_Bloodlines/status/1666403803090886658?t=KmKnUC_-Oe68zOfVnbnk2w&amp;s=19 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Rise, Kindred, and join us in September for a big announcement! </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <img width=\"800\" height=\"500\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/FyA44U8XwAEUDwv?format=jpg&amp;name=large\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/FyA44U8XwAEUDwv?format=jpg&amp;name=large\" data-thumb-url=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/FyA44U8XwAEUDwv?format=jpg&amp;name=large\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <i>Dear Bloodlines fans,<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been quite a while between updates while we\u2019ve had our heads down working on the game. We remain just as dedicated to delivering a great Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines game as we were when we announced, and are looking forward to showing you more in September this year.<br /> <br /> We acknowledge it was a long time ago that many of you pre-ordered Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2. As development continues, we will be updating the game\u2019s editions and bonus content, and we want to provide the best value to those of you who supported us via digital pre-order after all this time. We are thus offering refunds to anyone who has pre-ordered any edition of Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2. As part of this process, we are proactively refunding <b>all</b> pre-orders of physical products, including the Collector\u2019s Edition. The digital versions of the First Blood Edition, Unsanctioned Edition and Blood Moon Edition remain, but can be refunded if you choose.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re excited to show you more and hope to have all of you with us in September when we reveal more. We know you are eager to see how the game is coming along so we\u2019ve put together a fresh batch of <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2#post-alpha-in-game-screenshots\" target=\"_blank\"><u>screenshots</u></a> to share with you.<br /> <br /> For more information about refunds and how to submit your request, <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-juneupdate-faq\" target=\"_blank\">please visit our FAQ</a>.<br /> <br /> Until then, The Bloodlines Team</i><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T16:18:14-07:00","id":1514143,"title":"","content":"Announcement of an Announcement. The best kind of communicating with your public.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T16:57:10-07:00","id":1514145,"title":"","content":"Cool. I canceled my preorder after the whole Mitsoda thing. If the game ends up reviewing really well I could see myself buying it, but right now Paradox has a big hole to climb out of before I consider it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T18:26:43-07:00","id":1514151,"title":"","content":"Boy, studios are being slow to learn from Hi-Fi Rush's lessons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T19:09:06-07:00","id":1514153,"title":"","content":"What was the point of those specific screenshots? None of them really scream VTM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T20:07:04-07:00","id":1514154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514153#post1514153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was the point of those specific screenshots? None of them really scream VTM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I find them reminding me of VTMB1 locations but if they were made today and not nearly twenty years ago.<br /> <br /> ...And saying that out loud makes me feel old.<br /> <br /> The alley looks like the Downtown alleys. The ruined Asian Temple looks like it could be the Wan Kuei temple years after the end of the game. The underground area looks like the Nos Warrens and honestly looks like a Nos Warren period. The bar looks like it would fit right in with that high end hotel in Downtown. The basement hallway reminds me of the various sewers and the basement of the Ocean View.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T21:31:55-07:00","id":1514158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514154#post1514154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly I find them reminding me of VTMB1 locations but if they were made today and not nearly twenty years ago.<br /> <br /> ...And saying that out loud makes me feel old.<br /> <br /> The alley looks like the Downtown alleys. The ruined Asian Temple looks like it could be the Wan Kuei temple years after the end of the game. The underground area looks like the Nos Warrens and honestly looks like a Nos Warren period. The bar looks like it would fit right in with that high end hotel in Downtown. The basement hallway reminds me of the various sewers and the basement of the Ocean View.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really hope we're not going to find out that, surprise, they decided to switch the setting location back to LA. With all the abominable crunch such a last-minute shift would imply.<br /> <br /> It would be a totally stupid and incompetent thing to do. But the AAA games industry is nothing if not stupid and incompetent. (That, and cruel and greedy.)<br /> <br /> Realistically, this is unlikely. The game can (and probably will) suck for lots of reasons. I have no confidence in it at this point. (Especially with the idea of proactively canceling pre-orders. That sounds like a bad sign.). I just want it on record that, if a setting change DOES happen, I called it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T21:48:26-07:00","id":1514159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514153#post1514153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was the point of those specific screenshots? None of them really scream VTM.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume they are &quot;mood&quot; shots to compensate for the fact that they aren't willing to show any of the actual game yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514158#post1514158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really hope we're not going to find out that, surprise, they decided to switch the setting location back to LA. With all the abominable crunch such a last-minute shift would imply.<br /> <br /> It would be a totally stupid and incompetent thing to do. But the AAA games industry is nothing if not stupid and incompetent. (That, and cruel and greedy.)<br /> <br /> Realistically, this is unlikely. The game can (and probably will) suck for lots of reasons. I have no confidence in it at this point. (Especially with the idea of proactively canceling pre-orders. That sounds like a bad sign.). I just want it on record that, if a setting change DOES happen, I called it.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> The real question is how much of the original game is left and whether or not they have Chris Avellones and Mitsoda's material returned back into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T22:54:21-07:00","id":1514166,"title":"","content":"I may draw some flak here but while I liked Mitsoda's work in the original game, he wasn't necessary going to produce the same level this time.<br /> <br /> Times and people change. The fact that the Star Wars prequals made by George Lucas himself were not very good as compared to the original episodes IV-VI tells me that people that produced good stuff 10-15 years ago may no necessarily produce the same good stuff now.<br /> <br /> EDITED: And the screenshots looked pretty ok from a WoD mood kind of way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T23:02:00-07:00","id":1514167,"title":"","content":"I mean, the real question is, &quot;is the final product actually good?&quot;<br /> <br /> Plenty of the best video game publishers, and best video game makers, have put out duds Lots of people will buy whatever Hideo Kojima makes on his name alone... but that's not always a rewarding experience.<br /> <br /> The need to make sure it's actually a good game is increased with how long it's taken to make. It doesn't really matter what's happening behind the scenes. To general audiences if you're constantly delaying the game, they're going to want it to be better and better and better the more time it takes, because they've been burnt so many times on games taking forever and still being trash on release. Games can recover from a bad release (hey, speaking of Kojima...people really didn't like Death Stranding at first, but some patches and some time to adjust to the oddball premise, and people have warmed up to it enough it's getting a sequel now), but it's never a good place to put yourself.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, if BL2 is a great game despite not using a single bit of Mitsoda or Avellone's work? People aren't going to care about that. If it's not a great game, that will just be part of the autopsy of how a game squandered time, money, and fan dedication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T23:35:05-07:00","id":1514169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514151#post1514151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boy, studios are being slow to learn from Hi-Fi Rush's lessons.</div> </div> </div> </div>What lessons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T00:35:30-07:00","id":1514172,"title":"","content":"An announcement for an announcement is weak. That announcement in September better be something along the lines of &quot;And the game is gonna come out next week!&quot;. You don't need to build up hype for a game trapped in development-hell. Whatever they announce needs to offer some solid evidence that this is still a game anybody should be interested in. A couple of screenshots don't do that.<br /> <br /> The thing with this game is that since it has been trapped in development-hell the time we've spent waiting on more news doesn't necessarily equate to this game having gotten better. There was this recent <a href=\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-06-01/arcane-s-redfall-misfire-for-xbox-panned-after-7-5-billion-microsoft-deal\" target=\"_blank\">report on Redfall</a> detailing how mismanagement can really derail game-development to the point where after five years the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/node/1\" >Home</a> thing the developers on the project were hoping for was that the game would get canceled. And despite all the issues the leaders kept insisting everything would just come together in the final phase of development and they insisted on releasing it. So it got released and it has a 53 on Metacritic (and a 2.3 User-score) with barely anyone playing it at this point. It was a dud both in terms of reviews and sales.<br /> <br /> This could be the fate of Bloodlines 2 as well. That after all the confusion and chaos that trapped the game in development-hell, the released game can't be anything but a bit of a mess - no matter how much time has been spent on the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T01:29:03-07:00","id":1514175,"title":"","content":"'K then.<br /> <br /> That's about the most response I could muster for them. They hype died and rotted. I was willing to grit my teeth and power through motion sickness for the original Bloodlines 2, but if they keep the first-person pov only for this one then it'd have to be<i> damn good</i>, and what's there to be excited about when nothing about this game is known to form an opinion? I guess the tree is nice to look at?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T11:07:31-07:00","id":1514207,"title":"","content":"So I've been watching the WOD-news-show today with Outstar and even today she said she can't reveal who the new developer is which makes me think... That September-announcement is mostly about telling us who that is. And Outstar also said we shouldn't expect any other previews till September.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T11:29:47-07:00","id":1514212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514172#post1514172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An announcement for an announcement is weak. That announcement in September better be something along the lines of &quot;And the game is gonna come out next week!&quot;. You don't need to build up hype for a game trapped in development-hell. Whatever they announce needs to offer some solid evidence that this is still a game anybody should be interested in. A couple of screenshots don't do that.<br /> <br /> The thing with this game is that since it has been trapped in development-hell the time we've spent waiting on more news doesn't necessarily equate to this game having gotten better. There was this recent <a href=\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-06-01/arcane-s-redfall-misfire-for-xbox-panned-after-7-5-billion-microsoft-deal\" target=\"_blank\">report on Redfall</a> detailing how mismanagement can really derail game-development to the point where after five years the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/node/1\" >Home</a> thing the developers on the project were hoping for was that the game would get canceled. And despite all the issues the leaders kept insisting everything would just come together in the final phase of development and they insisted on releasing it. So it got released and it has a 53 on Metacritic (and a 2.3 User-score) with barely anyone playing it at this point. It was a dud both in terms of reviews and sales.<br /> <br /> This could be the fate of Bloodlines 2 as well. That after all the confusion and chaos that trapped the game in development-hell, the released game can't be anything but a bit of a mess - no matter how much time has been spent on the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Paradox actually STEPPED IN when the game was trapped in development hell and looked underwhelming. Which is a good thing.<br /> <br /> It means that they didn't just let the problem fester but moved it to a new studio.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T12:00:03-07:00","id":1514217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514212#post1514212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, Paradox actually STEPPED IN when the game was trapped in development hell and looked underwhelming. Which is a good thing.<br /> <br /> It means that they didn't just let the problem fester but moved it to a new studio.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily... It depends on what Paradox wants. I don't think one should look at what happened with Redfall and consider it a blueprint for what anyone involved in game-development should do (like the lesson there is to just do the opposite). There are more than enough game-studios that got shut down because the parent-company was very hands-on in what games they developed (Rare/Microsoft is a famous example of that).<br /> <br /> And I don't think all this kabuki-theater surrounding a simple question like &quot;Well, who's developing Bloolines 2?&quot; is a good PR-strategy. There's so much turnover in the videogames-industry these days and there are so many examples of game-studios with a good reputation producing stinkers (which then produce articles like the one about Redfall)... turning the reveal of some game-studio-name into an event is just such a pointless action at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T16:53:48-07:00","id":1514252,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the broader video-game audience has gotten wise to a lot of PR strategies to the point where these things are negatives now.<br /> <br /> Like, if you ask anyone who's favorite video game's developer was bought by Microsoft? They can warn you that the next game in their favorite franchise is now going to get released in a crappy state, and take a decade before the game is where it should have been at launch and recover fans for multiplayer to be fun if that's part of the game. Microsoft just has some really hated mandates it puts on the studios it buys because it actively makes game dev worse to help Microsoft's bottom line in the short term.<br /> <br /> If we look at the video games Paradox has started shopping out to other studios as they've grown out of just publishing their own work, there's some justifiable worry that part of the problem is Paradox's demands which can't be fixed by changing which studio is handling it. Some mandates from the owners that can sound very small, can turn any smaller studio's development process sour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T16:58:42-07:00","id":1514253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514158#post1514158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really hope we're not going to find out that, surprise, they decided to switch the setting location back to LA. With all the abominable crunch such a last-minute shift would imply.<br /> <br /> It would be a totally stupid and incompetent thing to do. But the AAA games industry is nothing if not stupid and incompetent. (That, and cruel and greedy.)<br /> <br /> Realistically, this is unlikely. The game can (and probably will) suck for lots of reasons. I have no confidence in it at this point. (Especially with the idea of proactively canceling pre-orders. That sounds like a bad sign.). I just want it on record that, if a setting change DOES happen, I called it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The third picture has a sign that says &quot;SEATTLE STR&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T19:40:03-07:00","id":1514266,"title":"","content":"The real question is given the development hell and how much politics has gotten involved in said development, will the game be better or worse than Redfall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T20:23:38-07:00","id":1514267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514207#post1514207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've been watching the WOD-news-show today with Outstar and even today she said she can't reveal who the new developer is which makes me think... That September-announcement is mostly about telling us who that is. And Outstar also said we shouldn't expect any other previews till September.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is certainly unusual. I can't think of too many times where a game is being worked on, but the company working on it hasn't been revealed yet. Nearly always, the studio is one of the first things revealed about a game, especially when it's an existing project being moved from one studio to another. In this case I don't know if it's good or bad, but it is incredibly strange.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T20:33:45-07:00","id":1514268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514166#post1514166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may draw some flak here but while I liked Mitsoda's work in the original game, he wasn't necessary going to produce the same level this time.<br /> <br /> Times and people change. The fact that the Star Wars prequals made by George Lucas himself were not very good as compared to the original episodes IV-VI tells me that people that produced good stuff 10-15 years ago may no necessarily produce the same good stuff now.<br /> <br /> EDITED: And the screenshots looked pretty ok from a WoD mood kind of way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Mitsoda's work was good, or not. But the problem is, they really hyped his being part of the team in the original advertising and this was a huge &quot;buy in&quot; for people who were deeply skeptical about some new studio making a sequel to a major cult classic that came out like 20 years ago. There were a number of people who would have panned the game, but were willing to give it a chance because Mitsoda was on it, and the company was saying that they had hired him specifically because they wanted to recreate and capture the feel of the original game. Then Mitsoda was unceremoniously booted to the curb in a way that made anyone who got on board because of Mitsoda, understandably upset.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't know if Star Wars is the best example. Episodes 1-3, while they had their problems, they had a coherent storyline and were much better than Episodes 7-9. At least my takeaway from Star Wars 1-9 is that letting the original creator produce stuff, even if it's not on the same level as the original, can still end up with something better than letting new people who aren't as invested in the material mangle it and toss out garbage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T20:54:44-07:00","id":1514269,"title":"","content":"It certainly sounds bad. What <i>good</i> reason would the publisher have for not revealing who's working on the game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T21:53:50-07:00","id":1514273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514269#post1514269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It certainly sounds bad. What <i>good</i> reason would the publisher have for not revealing who's working on the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it seems like the absolute best decision they could be making at this point and I'm surprised that so many fans are reacting negatively. No, actually, I take that back. I know why fans would feel that way but from a corporate perspective, I know exactly why they're doing it. After the PR Disaster that was having to shut down the previous studio for tanking the game (removing the content of its two major writers and thus 60% of the completed game is more or less confirmed as what happened), they clearly want to only announce the game's status when it's ready for release.<br /> <br /> We also know that the response to the finished content was lukewarm too. The controls were janky, the animation not exactly great, and response lukewarm.<br /> <br /> I can 100% get why Paradox wants the game up to the best possible look they can give it before sharing. This was meant to be their golden boy after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T02:28:54-07:00","id":1514285,"title":"","content":"Maybe they've announced an announcement which will in turn be that there is another announcement waiting on the horizon. <br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't get it. The original game on the source engine felt like an above average Half-Life 2 mod. Gunplay was shit and melee was jank. Yet for the most part the game was a blast. The story was pretty barebones too. The game shinned through characters and music, and it's not terribly difficult to structure a story like that. It's often compared to Deus ex, which again had shit graphics (for the time) shit combat and was hard-carried by character and setting. <br /> <br /> Essentially, the original game was great but it also sets a very low bar in most respects. The Devs don't need to be making something ultra ambitious. Once you've got a decent writer that understands the source material and a smattering of great voice actors it's not terribly difficult to do -Bloodlines, but better- . <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T05:52:51-07:00","id":1514301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514273#post1514273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean it seems like the absolute best decision they could be making at this point and I'm surprised that so many fans are reacting negatively. No, actually, I take that back. I know why fans would feel that way but from a corporate perspective, I know exactly why they're doing it. After the PR Disaster that was having to shut down the previous studio for tanking the game (removing the content of its two major writers and thus 60% of the completed game is more or less confirmed as what happened), they clearly want to only announce the game's status when it's ready for release.<br /> <br /> We also know that the response to the finished content was lukewarm too. The controls were janky, the animation not exactly great, and response lukewarm.<br /> <br /> I can 100% get why Paradox wants the game up to the best possible look they can give it before sharing. This was meant to be their golden boy after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>So why say anything if you don't have anything to say?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T10:57:22-07:00","id":1514320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514269#post1514269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It certainly sounds bad. What <i>good</i> reason would the publisher have for not revealing who's working on the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>A year or two back this was asked on a Paradox earnings call. To paraphrase the response, not revealing who\u2019s working on the game means they can focus on the game and don\u2019t have to deal with inquiries from fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T11:28:56-07:00","id":1514321,"title":"","content":"This has certainly been an interesting series of events, considering it was supposed to synergise to v5s release. With everything considered I'm watching with considerable interest.<br /> <br /> Although my pc is a brick so i probably won't be buying it lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T11:38:11-07:00","id":1514322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514320#post1514320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A year or two back this was asked on a Paradox earnings call. To paraphrase the response, not revealing who\u2019s working on the game means they can focus on the game and don\u2019t have to deal with inquiries from fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>If only Paradox had someone to employ who's job inherently deals with answering fans so the devs don't have too...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T15:37:18-07:00","id":1514346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514301#post1514301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So why say anything if you don't have anything to say?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because people had been thinking the game was cancelled-cancelled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514322#post1514322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If only Paradox had someone to employ who's job inherently deals with answering fans so the devs don't have too...</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel bad for Outstar because she often got sideswiped by this stuff herself. She actually played like 20 hours of the game before it was said it be nowhere near done.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T17:25:25-07:00","id":1514361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514346#post1514346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u2026I feel bad for Outstar because she often got sideswiped by this stuff herself. She actually played like 20 hours of the game before it was said it be nowhere near done.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Brian Mitsoda he was fired July 16th 2020. It wasn\u2019t announced for over a month. Seems kind of dismissive to think she didn\u2019t know about it and didn\u2019t play a role in how Paradox communicated it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T23:32:18-07:00","id":1514402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514273#post1514273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean it seems like the absolute best decision they could be making at this point and I'm surprised that so many fans are reacting negatively. No, actually, I take that back. I know why fans would feel that way but from a corporate perspective, I know exactly why they're doing it. After the PR Disaster that was having to shut down the previous studio for tanking the game (removing the content of its two major writers and thus 60% of the completed game is more or less confirmed as what happened), they clearly want to only announce the game's status when it's ready for release.<br /> <br /> We also know that the response to the finished content was lukewarm too. The controls were janky, the animation not exactly great, and response lukewarm.<br /> <br /> I can 100% get why Paradox wants the game up to the best possible look they can give it before sharing. This was meant to be their golden boy after all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> in the video game market, especially in the current period, that's a bullet shot in their foot. Announcements for announcement's sake is a red flag, so is not revealing the dev studio of a game.<br /> <br /> If anything, in the current period, the best decision is to be straight and honest with the players, and to cut the PR bullshit.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T23:48:06-07:00","id":1514403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514346#post1514346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel bad for Outstar because she often got sideswiped by this stuff herself. She actually played like 20 hours of the game before it was said it be nowhere near done.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Outstar certainly isn't in an enviable position here. But it's not like this is the community's fault. Fans are curious what's going on but the only person from Paradox that's talking to them is... Outstar. And unsurprisingly &quot;Just don't say anything for years.&quot; isn't a very good PR-strategy. People starting to believe the game is unofficially already dead is also a result of that. And just repeatedly telling the community &quot;I can't tell you anything.&quot; doesn't make it seem like Outstar is engaging in any sort of dialogue either. Of course, she's just the face of this bad PR-strategy in this situation.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T00:15:40-07:00","id":1514413,"title":"","content":"As someone relatively young in the PR industry, I don't envy her position, but part of her job is telling her higher ups that the PR strategy is crap and there's no way she can spin it otherwise. It's not a great thing, but lots and lots of people in her position, across lots of different industries (and even other parts of society than industry) have left jobs because their good name as an honest communicator is more important to their long term career than shilling for people that don't have her back with substantive things she can use to help smooth this period over.<br /> <br /> An unfortunately reality of the PR world, is that most companies view their PR people as the first people to throw under the bus if things are going bad. Weighing the reality of either losing all credibility because you keep letting yourself take the fall for other people, or the reality of losing an awesome job without a backup and the stress of that uncertainty is a shit place to be....<br /> <br /> But this is Paradox's fault. If she opts to stay on the Paradox train despite seeing way more problems than we do because it's her job to try to fix them on some level, she's stuck going where the tracks lead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T03:15:44-07:00","id":1514438,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't really buy the idea that Paradox just can't walk and chew bubble gum at the same time. Especially when one is just &quot;communicate the state of development&quot;. While not without work involved, drafting a public statement about an ongoing process, it's orders of magnitude more manageable than making a video game. Especially if, as stated, they have or could have people whose JOB is to interface with the public. What are you paying PR for if not to do that work for you?<br /> <br /> Either something's wrong with PR itself, or there's something wrong with the game. Either way, it doesn't imply the ship is sailing well.<br /> <br /> Moreover, whatever problems might be going on behind closed doors, NOT talking about them is arguably worse (that is, unless what's going on is really, <i>criminally</i> bad). We can imagine worse than the reality. And not talking about the state of the game means you're not really exercising control of the situation.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> (To use an example: back in 2015, when Games Workshop was shuttering Warhammer Fantasy Battles with a bullet and rebooting it with Age of Sigmar, the company at the time had ZERO online presence. No blog, no newsletter, no social media. In <b>2015</b>. The only information they put out, after they destroyed WHFB's setting with an apocalypse, was ONE ad in White Dwarf, a print magazine, saying that Age of Sigmar was coming. And then total radio silence. For SIX MONTHS. GW basically let a fanbase that was already mad about the End Times stew in their own rage for half a year. Talking to each other online and in game stores, with no input or intervention from the company. Even if AoS's initial release build wasn't hot trash, the negative reception from fans was all but inevitable. It was so bad that not only did AoS require a complete overhaul just to make it playable, let alone good, it got GW's management <b>fired</b> due to how badly they messed things up. That almost never happens, bad bosses taking the fall for their mistakes. THAT is what happens when you refuse to communicate with your customers.)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T03:24:16-07:00","id":1514439,"title":"","content":"Yeah, one idea I had is that what was actually important about this &quot;announcement of an announcement&quot; was the message of them auto-canceling/refunding all physical pre-orders. And the intent there is to set the stage to reveal a rather different type of videogame in September. Like, for example, let's say the new developer is Chinese Room and for the last couple of years this new iteration of Bloodlines 2 is now a walking-simulator mostly reliant on environmental storytelling. And that's why they also couldn't show any gameplay-footage or reveal more information because they would have to admit at that point that the glimpses we got in the past of Bloodlines 2 have actually very little to do with this new version that will come out (and yet still be called Bloodlines 2).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T03:44:45-07:00","id":1514443,"title":"","content":"Ah. And to avoid legal liability, they're ensuring that preorders are refunded. Because otherwise, they'd be asking people to give their money to a product that's not the one they asked for/were sold on.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, it looks like a very nice set of patio furniture. No, I'm not paying for that, because I asked for a <i>boat</i>.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T11:05:45-07:00","id":1514484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514361#post1514361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to Brian Mitsoda he was fired July 16th 2020. It wasn\u2019t announced for over a month. Seems kind of dismissive to think she didn\u2019t know about it and didn\u2019t play a role in how Paradox communicated it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I do think she's not in the loop for a lot of this stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514142-paradox-will-make-a-bloodlines-2-announcement-in-september?p=1514443#post1514443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. And to avoid legal liability, they're ensuring that preorders are refunded. Because otherwise, they'd be asking people to give their money to a product that's not the one they asked for/were sold on.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, it looks like a very nice set of patio furniture. No, I'm not paying for that, because I asked for a <i>boat</i>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the fact they're NOT refunding the Digital Orders is the bigger clue there.<br /> <br /> Which means that all of the content in the Digital Orders will still be present in the main game.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://gamepreorders.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://gamepreorders.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://gamepreorders.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2\" target=\"_blank\"> https://gamepreorders.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This stuff is still available:<br /> <br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1251_1686420568996_629\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1251\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1251\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1251&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b<br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1252_1686420587